Semantic class hierarchy:
	Dispatcher

		Comparator
			Unary_Comparator
			Binary_Comparator
				Commutative_Binary_Comparator
				Non_Commutative_Binary_Comparator
			Set_Comparator
				Commutative_Set_Comparator
				Non_Commutative_Set_Comparator

		Transformer
		Resolver
		Filter
		Evaluator
			Priority_Evaluator
			Score_Evaluator
		Classifier
			Feature_Analyzer
			Group_Classifier

		Processor
		Iterator

		Computer

	Regulations

	Aggregator
		Group_Organizer
		Sorter

	Generator



Roles:
	Abstract Class: Dispatcher
		Abstract Class: Comparator
			Class: Unary_Comparator
				Brief: Perform a comparison of a single item

			Class: Binary_Comparator
				Brief: Perform a comparison of two items

			Abstract Class: Set_Comparator
				Class: Commutative_Set_Comparator
					Brief: Perform a commutative comparison of a set of items
				Class: Non_Commutative_Set_Comparator
					Brief: Perform a non commutative comparison of a set of items

		Abstract Class: Transformer
			Class: Evaluator
				Brief: Perform evaluation of an item
				Class: Priority_Evaluator
					Brief: Evaluate priority of an item
				Class: Score_Evaluator
					Brief: Compute a score for an item
			Class: Resolver
				Brief: Resolve an item into a value
			Abstract Class: Classifier
				Class: Feature_Analyzer
					Brief: Analyze multiple features of an item an return a report object
				Class: Group_Classifier
					Brief: Classify an item into one of several groups

			Class: Processor
				Brief: Perform one or multiple actions on an item
				Class: Strict_Processor
					Brief: Under the condition that only one rule of the regulations matches the item an action is performed on an item
					Note: There could be various strict options of other semantic classes here as well.

		Class: Iterator
			Brief: Iterate over an item and yield sub items
			Class: Filter
				Brief: Iterate over an item and conditionally yield sub items


Note: Let's try to break down these items into specific features